{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1070317-the-tone-of-scion","id":1070317,"title":"The Tone of Scion","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-29T14:56:25-07:00","id":1070317,"title":"The Tone of Scion","content":"What do you think the general tone of Scion should be? I've heard a lot of different answers for this so i wanted them all in the same place.<br /> <br /> As for my opinion, part of the reason i loved scion in the first place was that it wasnt like WoD or CofD in that it wasn't that gritty or as dark, which in my humble opinion it shouldn't be. I always thought Scion should be &quot;our world&quot; (tone wise that is) with gods, instead of another World of Darkness, or a Trinity-esque World of Brightness, or even the weird mix that is Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13001-sdespencer","name":"SdeSpencer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T15:47:26-07:00","id":1070352,"title":"","content":"I have spent a lot of time sitting here and trying to think of what the tone of Scion is, and, I don't think it quite has one. Scion facilitates a ton of different stories with wildly different tones, very much up to the Storyteller. What I think unifies these divergent games is a theme however, the theme of Power. You are a Scion, and you shake the world as you walk. If you want, you can bend Nations to the breaking point, shatter physical laws, change the world. And yet, you are dwarfed by your parents, changing the world means nothing to beings such as Atum-Ra who can end all of reality by simply blinking.<br /> <br /> The most common tone I have seen used for Scion, and the one I like the most is relatively dark, with an incredible sense of hope lingering just over the horizon. The world of Scion is pretty dark, it is our world, but All Myths are True. Mortals by and large likely don't realize how dark the world is, but Scions will know. Reality is ordered by, by and large, colossally powerful, and uncaring entities. Very, <i>very</i> few Deities give a damn about Mortals. Sure, they might have a favorite mortal, and they will likely love their Scions in a culturally appropriate way, but mortals are gnats. To the Tuatha, the Sons of Mil are uppity, Deicidal invaders who colonized <i>their</i> island. To the Theoi, the mortals are creatures whose lives pass in a blink, and mean little to Olympus short of occasionally being play things. To the Anunna, mortals are a slave race, destined for a horrific afterlife from which there is no escape. To the Thousand Gods of Hatti, mortals are annoying little creatures who need to grovel more, least they be brought to extinction, all while serving their will.<br /> <br /> Now, your everyday mortal probably doesn't quite grasp this, but for a Scion, they get to see the world is big, and scary. In life, some Scions get to be aware how close reality is to collapsing on frequent occasions. The Netjer have a nightly battle to preserve reality, the Teotl have one to preserve the world. To the Bogovi, you get to know that <i>you, </i>personally, are a flaw in the system, an aberration that should not be. A Scion of the Shen gets to know that Tian will shift in opinion, and The Mandate of Heaven will be given to a new authority, and there will be chaos in time. The Aesir just get to be gloomy because they know an End is on it's way. Theoi Scions get to know that The Son will be here some day, and will have to start planning on tossing their parents in a giant prison, or getting tossed in there themselves too. Mortals don't really know, grasp, or have to deal with these issues, but they are forefront in the realities of Scions.<br /> <br /> In death, an alarming number of mortals are doomed to a depressing existence for all eternity as well. To use myself as an example, I will run through the big Pantheons and what my personal fate would be in Scion's world in relation to death.<ul><li><b>Aesir</b>: I am sure as hell not meeting the 'Die in Battle' clause, so I'm off to Hel's hall, and that's... not fun. I think I will also get press-ganged into fighting at Ragnarok for Loki.</li> <li><b>Anunna</b>: I am off to Irkalla, so, that means I am going to forget who I was, and be eternally stuck in a state of starving and dying of thirst since I doubt anyone is going to think of giving me sacrifices.</li> <li><b>Bogovi</b>: Not that bad actually, they have a nice underworld under Veles. Gets a bit spooky for a bit in Winter, and I'll have to get used to being used to help with Veles' cattle for all eternity. Or, well, until Svarog wakes up and ends reality to give it another go.</li> <li><b>Deva</b>: I don't know enough to be sure of how this would work, Samudra might be able to pop in and toss his thoughts in. Reincarnation, but I don't know how hot my next life would be. I am destined to eventually climb the ladder though, so that's nice.</li> <li><b>Kami</b>: Got a few choices. Yomi is perpetually dark and doesn't seem to be too fun with Izanami hanging around. Based on the very little we know, I don't think I'd be happy with perpetually decaying. Ne-no-Kuni would <i>not</i> be awesome since I don't deal well with bogs, snakes, wasps, or centipedes. Jigoku would mean reincarnation at some point, but <i>man</i> some of those tortures are horrific.</li> <li><b>Netjer</b>: I... don't know how my heart would be weighed. The fact I am going to probably not be entombed with a Book of Going Forth by Day means I'll have to be basing my travels through Duat off what I can remember, and due to that, and generally not living up to ancient Egyptian moral standards, I don't know how many gates I would be able to get through. I don't think I would reach Osiris paradise at the end of the desert.</li> <li><b>Orisha</b>: We don't really know much if anything about their Underworld situation, so, might be nice! Might be bad.</li> <li><b>Shen</b>: Similar sort of situation to Jigoku with the Kami. Reincarnation yes, horrific tortures, spooky.</li> <li><b>Teotl</b>: Since I'm probably not going to be sacrificed to one of the Teotl, or die a warrior's death serving the Empire, I'm off to Mictlan which is just not fun ever.</li> <li><b>Theoi</b>: I'm not interesting enough to get thrown into Tartaros or the Elysian Fields, so I'm off to Asphodel which is very much a perpetual boredom afterlife. Also I will forget who I was and everything I knew due to the Lethe, not great. If I was inducted into a Mystery Cult, might have a better time, but they're not really advertising.</li> <li><b>Tuatha</b>: We don't really know what was going on here, but I might sneak into Inis Locha as a possible descendant of Mil. So, I'll be living like it's Iron Age Ireland for eternity. It's okay, a lot like the Bogovi situation. Would get to talk to all the dead Gods about the place, so that would be neat.</li> </ul>So, I don't have an awesome chance of getting a decent Afterlife, which is in most cases the rest of every mortal for all eternity. Doesn't sound fun, and that's pretty grim. While mortals may not really grasp this, or know this, Scions do. Great motivation for many Pantheon's Scions is desperately making a break for Apotheosis to escape the horrible afterlife waiting for them. In addition to this, Scions frequently make bad decisions, level cities, get in fights with abstract personifications of reality, they tend not to have fun lives. Eventful lives, yes, fun, not necessarily. Probably lots of really high highs, and really low lows.<br /> <br /> However, this grim darkness is not what sells Scion for me. It is the overwhelming brightness that <i>can</i> be, just waiting in the wings. You are the Son of Marduk, and you are kind, and gentle. You look out at Irkalla and go, &quot;I can change this.&quot; You can bring relief, and mercy to all those eons of dead mortals. You can take your father aside, and try to teach him mercy, and kindness, to respect mortals and understand them. Or maybe just convince the mortals to make their own slave race of robots and continue the Mesopotamian divine pyramid scheme.<br /> <br /> Scion is, at least in my games, and the games I have played in, a fairly dark game. But you can change that, you can make the world so much better. You can rewrite reality, and you could change that darkness into light.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T17:50:20-07:00","id":1070406,"title":"","content":"I generally see Scion as a game that is as dark as human reality or the various worlds humans (at the very least) think they happen to live in. So you know, pretty dark but generally not in a Grimdark Warhammer 40K kinda way. There is room for hope and improvement, but also suffering and disaster. I do reject the notion of Scion embodying a Noblebright PG rated setting however. This is a setting in which people practice blood sacrifice to placate and empower very real deities.<br /> <br /> <br /> Watcher: While it doesn't really change your point, the idea that its either Valhalla or Hel is a misunderstanding (mostly...). There are many other potential afterlives in Alfheim or the various halls of other gods. Granted it kinda resembles the Egyptian example of &quot;Not likely to live up to Nordic Standards&quot;, but its a possibility. Also Reincarnation is a thing along family lines, but only for some aspects of the soul, so its not really a complete &quot;You&quot;. Which now that i think about it....might be another layer of fridge horror for modern people....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T18:02:54-07:00","id":1070409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1070317-the-tone-of-scion?p=1070406#post1070406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Watcher: While it doesn't really change your point, the idea that its either Valhalla or Hel is a misunderstanding (mostly...). There are many other potential afterlives in Alfheim or the various halls of other gods. Granted it kinda resembles the Egyptian example of &quot;Not likely to live up to Nordic Standards&quot;, but its a possibility. Also Reincarnation is a thing along family lines, but only for some aspects of the soul, so its not really a complete &quot;You&quot;. Which now that i think about it....might be another layer of fridge horror for modern people....</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds very interesting, I have never heard of Alfheim functioning as an afterlife, or any Hall asides from F\u00f3lkvangr having an afterlife component! Where does that come up? That sounds very interesting in the least, and I would love to read the appropriate section of the Eddas. I am always striving to get a more solid grasp on the Aesir, though they are not my particular cup of tea, they are one of the Pantheons the general public has the most connection to outside of the Theoi or their own cultural background.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T20:05:39-07:00","id":1070458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SdeSpencer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1070317-the-tone-of-scion#post1070317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you think the general tone of Scion should be? I've heard a lot of different answers for this so i wanted them all in the same place.<br /> <br /> As for my opinion, part of the reason i loved scion in the first place was that it wasnt like WoD or CofD in that it wasn't that gritty or as dark, which in my humble opinion it shouldn't be. I always thought Scion should be &quot;our world&quot; (tone wise that is) with gods, instead of another World of Darkness, or a Trinity-esque World of Brightness, or even the weird mix that is Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Actually, there is quite a lot of opportunity for Scion to be dark and gritty if you know where to look. Greek mythology is notorious for its love of tragedies, often with Heroes and villains being the cause of their own downfall. And one could argue that any member of the Norse pantheon is at risk of being seized by nihilism once the reality of their Fate finally sinks in. Plus, there are TONS of stories throughout nearly every mythos that involve elements of genocide, rape, slavery, torture, maiming, war, betrayal and so on. Just because it's more set on a modern fantasy environment doesn't mean it's any less gruesome than Chronicles of Darkness.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> -----------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> But personally, I like the idea of Scion being similar to an &quot;Old vs New&quot; mentality. In which the various mythical beings throughout history prefer the old ways (xenophobia, classism, gender roles, est) and expect their descendants to adhere to them, while those who have grown up in a modern environment find such ideologies to be outdated and backwards. As a result, the Scions have two options available: They can rebel against the status quo and bring about much needed change to the system, or they can go with the flow in order to avoid drawing the ire of entities far more powerful than them.<br /> <br /> Of course, there was already a thread on here that got into a great big argument over whether or not the pantheons would change their views simply because mortals told them it was wrong. I take one glance at both modern and ancient religion and conclude that is an extremely long shot to say the least.<br /> <br /> <br /> But what if the next generation decided to do things differently? Zeus was raised by a Titan (Gaia) and he didn't just stop at getting revenge against Chronus, he turned his vengeance upon all the Titans, including Gaia. What if somebody were to supplant Zeus and attempt diplomatic negotiations, instead of furthering a millennia old grudge? What if somebody gave Gaia what she wanted and accepted her children onto Olympus as equals, rather than slaves?<br /> <br /> I think the reason why the Titan War is as bad as it is, is because the ancient grand parents are too stuck in their ways to admit they were in the wrong. It's up to the new generation to bury the hatchet and set things right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-29-2017, 11:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T20:21:51-07:00","id":1070462,"title":"","content":"The fact that 2e is shipping with three Modes in the corebook and several coming later on indicates that there is no central tone of Scion. If you want superheroes with a mythological theme, it's right there for you, but you can just as easily do melodramatic clashes between tradition and the modern world, intimate personal journeys about building an identity for yourself instead of being defined by expectations set by others, you could do crime noir if you really wanted.<br /> <br /> I know that at my table, it's going to be upbeat queer urban fantasy. There is faith and hope and power, where the divine is real and there to empower the willful to do great deeds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T20:30:11-07:00","id":1070463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1070317-the-tone-of-scion?p=1070352#post1070352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bunch of shitty afterlife stuff</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As a Scion, you also have the option of carving out your own version of the afterlife that can be as appalling or as pleasant as you want. Heck, you could do away with the concept of punishment all together. <i>Heaven's a party and everyone's invited!</i> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Of course, I'm certainly no better than you when it comes to those possibilities, though if I had to pick one, I'd probably go with the Netjer. Failing the feather test doesn't sound so bad if the punishment is that I simply cease to exist.<br /> <br /> No consciousness means no torment; so I'd be at peace either way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-29-2017, 11:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T00:49:03-07:00","id":1070516,"title":"","content":"The tone can shift wildly in Scion without any of it being wrong, sometimes within a single campaign or even session. A karaoke contest with Bragi gets interrupted by a hydra crashing through the wall and after the climactic fight you realize a scion of Artemis kidnapped your love interest in the confusion and will give them back if you pull a mission impossible style heist against a company owned by a scion of Quetzcoatl. Then they go back on their word, kill them anyway, and it becomes a tragic revenge arc.<br /> <br /> In there sheer vastness of human religion and mythology there are stories that are heartwarming, ones that are horrifying. I'd say only real constant in Scion is the idea of potential abuse of power, unasked for burdens and dealing with sometimes troublesome on an apocalyptic scale family.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T04:23:43-07:00","id":1070567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1070317-the-tone-of-scion?p=1070409#post1070409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That sounds very interesting, I have never heard of Alfheim functioning as an afterlife, or any Hall asides from F\u00f3lkvangr having an afterlife component! Where does that come up? That sounds very interesting in the least, and I would love to read the appropriate section of the Eddas. I am always striving to get a more solid grasp on the Aesir, though they are not my particular cup of tea, they are one of the Pantheons the general public has the most connection to outside of the Theoi or their own cultural background.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of it just isn't in the Poetic and Prose Edda, which is probably why the vast majority of people get those kinds of impressions. For the Alfar we are talking about hard scholarship, literary review and linguistics. Basically in a nutshell, there is rather significant evidence that many of the Alfar are literally the souls of dead ancestors who achieved some sort of greatness in life and that the religious rituals surrounding them constitute a very private ancestral cult. Olaf Geirstad-Alf is a good example of someone explicitly identified as having become an Alfar after death.<br /> <br /> As for the others, I always recommend Wilhelm Gronbech's &quot;Culture of the Teutons&quot; for some serious looks into the fundamentals of the worldview, culture and faith. <a href=\"http://northvegr.org/secondary%20sources/religion%20culture%20history/the%20culture%20of%20the%20teutons/index.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://northvegr.org/secondary%20sou...ons/index.html</a> (Though i would warn you, we are back at the serious scholarship level and alot of the information is across multiple chapters.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T04:33:41-07:00","id":1070568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1070317-the-tone-of-scion?p=1070352#post1070352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]<b>Orisha</b>: We don't really know much if anything about their Underworld situation, so, might be nice! Might be bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>We <i>do</i> know that they don't have an underworld, in fact. All the dead go to dwell in the heavenly city/village Orun Rere, where Olodumare and the Orisha also live (imagine a division between the normal city and the palace circuit here). The most exalted of the dead are the ancestors, those who led a exemplary life, died of ripe old age, and continue to be venerated by their descendants; those can send part of their life force to &quot;partially reincarnate&quot; as a new person in their blood line. The other dead get assigned plots of land and other privileges in the city according to their virtue and their life span (thus suicides, who cut their life span short, get significantly shitty plots of land). The very worst are thrown onto the midden heap of the city, the &quot;Heaven of Potsherds&quot; Orun Apadi, although it has been suggested that this &quot;hell&quot; is a later interpolation in Yoruba lore caused by Abrahamic influence. There's a lot more detail to be mentioned about Orun, but I think that gives a good idea of what <i>tone</i> the Yoruba afterlife has.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1070317-the-tone-of-scion?p=1070409#post1070409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That sounds very interesting, I have never heard of Alfheim functioning as an afterlife, or any Hall asides from F\u00f3lkvangr having an afterlife component! Where does that come up? That sounds very interesting in the least, and I would love to read the appropriate section of the Eddas. I am always striving to get a more solid grasp on the Aesir, though they are not my particular cup of tea, they are one of the Pantheons the general public has the most connection to outside of the Theoi or their own cultural background.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alfheim I've never heard of as well, but I'm always open to be corrected. One alternative I still have in mind is the palace of Aegir and Ran at the bottom of the sea; Ran is said to catch men at sea with her net and drag them down, and whether that is just a metaphor for drowning (Ran is a very metaphorical being in general) or means that her home is an underworld for the drowned is pretty up to interpretation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T04:37:03-07:00","id":1070569,"title":"","content":"My idea is: <br /> <br /> Scion can really be everything<br /> <br /> I played it in very different style. <br /> <br /> - In MidleAge ( epic fantasy style, the real hero of the legends or vykings)<br /> - 1930 in america ( with a very deep noir tone, blackjack, alcohol and sigaretts, bossess issues etcetc)<br /> - Our days with all the light and dark of our community<br /> <br /> But what i prefer is... THE PULP ONE. Fuck i love pulp scion. Is like tarantino making a superhero movie, i just love it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","name":"ElanConnor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T07:10:10-07:00","id":1070619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElanConnor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1070317-the-tone-of-scion?p=1070569#post1070569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My idea is:<br /> <br /> Scion can really be everything<br /> <br /> I played it in very different style.<br /> <br /> - In MidleAge ( epic fantasy style, the real hero of the legends or vykings)<br /> - 1930 in america ( with a very deep noir tone, blackjack, alcohol and sigaretts, bossess issues etcetc)<br /> - Our days with all the light and dark of our community<br /> <br /> But what i prefer is... THE PULP ONE. Fuck i love pulp scion. Is like tarantino making a superhero movie, i just love it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> If you do one focused around the Asian pantheons, you can even make a Wire Fu setting with people jumping around through the air, clashing blades and magic as they pass!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T08:40:07-07:00","id":1070670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1070317-the-tone-of-scion?p=1070567#post1070567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most of it just isn't in the Poetic and Prose Edda, which is probably why the vast majority of people get those kinds of impressions. For the Alfar we are talking about hard scholarship, literary review and linguistics. Basically in a nutshell, there is rather significant evidence that many of the Alfar are literally the souls of dead ancestors who achieved some sort of greatness in life and that the religious rituals surrounding them constitute a very private ancestral cult. Olaf Geirstad-Alf is a good example of someone explicitly identified as having become an Alfar after death.<br /> <br /> As for the others, I always recommend Wilhelm Gronbech's &quot;Culture of the Teutons&quot; for some serious looks into the fundamentals of the worldview, culture and faith. <a href=\"http://northvegr.org/secondary%20sources/religion%20culture%20history/the%20culture%20of%20the%20teutons/index.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://northvegr.org/secondary%20sou...ons/index.html</a> (Though i would warn you, we are back at the serious scholarship level and alot of the information is across multiple chapters.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, okay, that's actually quite interesting. And no worries about the scholarship thing, I am doing my Masters in Irish Mythology, so scholarly work doesn't bug me. I have got a folder filled with articles discussing Ashanti religious systems secreted away for the next few weeks of reading for myself. With Irish mythology, that late 19th century, early 20th century period is normally a huge red flag for dodgy scholarship, but I will dig into Gronbech and the consensus about him. Thanks very much!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T09:32:26-07:00","id":1070697,"title":"","content":"I always saw it as &quot;slightly darkish, but very heroic, and sometimes rather surreal&quot;. If that makes any sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T09:32:34-07:00","id":1070698,"title":"","content":"Gronbech is hardly someone to be concerned about in the same way you would want to treat Crowley or Guido Von List. He is perhaps the best respected Cultural and Theological Historian of the period and certainly the most influential in his native Denmark for even decades afterwards. To quote: He was unusually capable of immersing himself in the system of thought he wished to depict,such that in the words of his English-language biographer he could &quot;write about [it] as if he accepted its theses and principles&quot;, and &quot;it is not possible to circumscribe accurately what his own religious\u2014not to mention political\u2014convictions must have been.&quot;<br /> <br /> He writes in that long winded, academic, turn of the century style that tends to put people off, but if your familiar with the style of scholarship then i would highly recommend him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T12:05:29-07:00","id":1070783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1070317-the-tone-of-scion?p=1070352#post1070352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]<b>Deva</b>: I don't know enough to be sure of how this would work, Samudra might be able to pop in and toss his thoughts in. Reincarnation, but I don't know how hot my next life would be. I am destined to eventually climb the ladder though, so that's nice.</div> </div> </div> </div>You called? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> There are technically two kinds of Death in Hinduism, so you have two possible outcomes.<br /> <br /> The first is the Death overseen by Yama (or, in a more general sense, Indra and his court), which is the typical 'You die, you are judged by Yama, Lord of the Underworld, and given your just deserts'. What exactly this is, varies by telling. In some beliefs, you are punished for your sins in Naraka, or given your rewards in Svarga and then sent onto your next life. In others, the quality of your next life IS your reward and/or punishment. (I'll also make a quick note here that time is an illusion in Hinduism so your 'past' life could very well be from the future...so your punishment for evil in this life may be to be reborn during the time of the Black Death or something). In other tellings, part of the reward and punishment is handled during life itself, administered by Shani, God of misfortune and step-brother of Yama.<br /> <br /> As for what decides whether you get rewarded or punished, well that varies from 'don't be a jerk' to 'carefully and to the letter follow the rules and regulations set out for your caste and sub-caste till the end of your days to maintain purity'. There are descriptions of Naraka that are almost Inferno-esque, describing various realms dedicated to punishing various sins. Eating beef and killing cows is a popular feature on these lists of sins (of course Indra in the Vedas eats beef like there's no tomorrow but most Hindus nowadays really don't like to think about their holiest of holy books describing beef eating, but I digress). If you have ever eaten beef then you are probably on a one-way ticket to the absolute depths of Naraka <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Of course I'll probably be meeting you there for the exact same reason <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Those people living it up in Svarga getting rewarded are the Pitri, the honoured ancestors...Hindu funeral rites often end with a prayer that the departed soul join the Pitri. (Pitri, incidentally, literally means Fathers; no one particularly talks about what happens to the women getting rewarded, because orthodox Hinduism is nothing if not patriarchal).<br /> <br /> Now, the second kind of Death, is the Death overseen by Shiva and Kali (or, in a more general sense, the Trimurti and Tridevi), the death of liberation. It is tied not to morality or virtue, but to enlightenment. Through Yoga, be it the meditative practices of Ashtanga Yoga (a.k.a. the stuff most westerners recognize as Yoga), the search of knowledge and Truth that is Jnana Yoga, the carrying out of sacred duties (which again may be defined by caste roles but need not be) of Karma Yoga, or absolute loving Devotion to Divinity that is Bhakti Yoga, the seeker recognizes and understands Brahman, the underlying Truth of Reality, and becomes one with it...exactly what that means has a lot of variations and personal interpretations, but whatever it is it always includes being freed from the cycle of reincarnation...you are no longer bound by the Lie of Heaven and Hell, you have Ascended to the Supernal (to borrow some imagery from another gameline entirely <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ).<br /> <br /> If you can manage that, well, you're set.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T02:31:02-07:00","id":1071139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1070317-the-tone-of-scion?p=1070783#post1070783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you have ever eaten beef then you are probably on a one-way ticket to the absolute depths of Naraka <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Of course I'll probably be meeting you there for the exact same reason <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sorry, but I just don't think spiritual enlightenment is worth giving up steak and burgers!<br /> <br /> Also, I'm rather curious to know what constitutes as evil deeds in Hinduism, since there is a sect of practitioners who specifically focus on disillusioning themselves of EVERYTHING (including the consumption of human flesh and feces) in order that they might view the world without biased judgement.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zqZQesGmpIk\" data-code=\"zqZQesGmpIk\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/zqZQesGmpIk/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-31-2017, 05:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T04:37:59-07:00","id":1071183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1070317-the-tone-of-scion?p=1071139#post1071139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Sorry, but I just don't think spiritual enlightenment is worth giving up steak and burgers!</div> </div> </div> </div>You won't have to <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> As I mentioned in my earlier post, giving up steak and burgers is only a requirement for entering Heaven...not spiritual enlightenment. The goal of spiritual enlightenment is to transcend both Heaven and Hell and achieve Liberation. Eating beef is a Sin, and therefore tied to Morality, whereas Enlightenment is separate from Morality. Morality only determines whether you go to Heaven or Hell and what form you come back in...and both Heaven and Hell are Fail States as far as Hinduism is concerned.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1070317-the-tone-of-scion?p=1071139#post1071139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I'm rather curious to know what constitutes as evil deeds in Hinduism, since there is a sect of practitioners who specifically focus on disillusioning themselves of EVERYTHING (including the consumption of human flesh and feces) in order that they might view the world without biased judgement.</div> </div> </div> </div>'Evil deeds' ranges from 'being a jerk' to 'marrying outside your sub-caste' to 'eating beef' to murder to 'all non-procreative sex' to theft to adultery depending on which Hindu you ask or which text you refer to... I'm pretty certain nobody's come up with a proper official listing, and Hinduism having no central authority there probably never will be. And again, this really doesn't matter because Sin itself is a part of the Lie of the World, of Avidya Maya, the Ignorance of Illusion. The Aghori that you're referring to ARE sinning as far as most Hindus are concerned...they just don't care because their focus is not Morality but Enlightenment. Funnily enough, the word Aghori literally means 'Not Terrible', and they took that name because they want to point out that the practices they indulge in are only 'terrible' through the eyes of civilized society, not in the face of Ultimate Truth.<br /> <br /> They're not the only ones, Tantrik mystics who worship Kali explicitly use what they call the five Ms (Matsya, meaning fish, Mansa, meaning meat, Madya, meaning alcohol, Mudrika, meaning parched rice, and Maithun, meaning sexual intercourse) in their rituals to honor Kali specifically because Orthodox Hinduism considers these five things unclean, and goes to great lengths to keep them away from temples and other 'holy' things, and by using them in the worship of God(dess) the Tantrik shows that he has overcome this limitation imposed by society. One Tantra inspired hymn to the Goddess even calls her Mahadevi, Mahasuri...i.e., she who is both The Great (Maha) Goddess (Devi) and The Great Demoness (Asuri)...or, to use Scion terms, the Great Goddess and the Great Titaness, with the implication being that both what orthodox Hinduism terms 'holy' and all it terms 'unholy' arise from the same Divinity.<br /> <br /> Interestingly, for all their otherwise bizarre practices, Aghoris and Tantriks are usually thoroughly opposed to the Caste System that Orthodox Hinduism is so fond of...all members of all castes including the untouchables are welcome, as both students and teachers (like most of Hinduism, these groups have strong teacher-student traditions). Tantra goes a step further, and allows women to be both teachers and priestesses, something Orthodox Hinduism does not allow, and in rural parts of India it is not unheard of for women and untouchables to join these sects as a way to get away from the mistreatment meted out to them on a daily basis. It's been getting better in recent years, but for a long time the only way a woman would have gotten any respect in a typical patriarchal village would have been living in the cremation grounds and covering herself with ashes while drinking out of a human skull <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (BTW, that was a pretty excellent video and the guy did some good research <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I especially love that he points out that Hatha/Ashtanga Yoga pretty much IS Yoga as far as the West is concerned <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> when there's so many Paths to Enlightenment)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1344,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","user":"Samudra","date":". 03-31-2017, 09:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T06:37:29-07:00","id":1071221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1070317-the-tone-of-scion?p=1071183#post1071183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> (BTW, that was a pretty excellent video and the guy did some good research <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I especially love that he points out that Hatha/Ashtanga Yoga pretty much IS Yoga as far as the West is concerned <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> when there's so many Paths to Enlightenment)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, he does a lot of culture videos across video games. He also has a video talking about historically accurate Ninjas, since he used to live in Japan right next door to Iga (the birth place of Ninjutsu).<br /> <br /> Not sure if you've played Nioh, but that scene where the guy uses his cat like a pocket watch is actually semi relevent to ninjas! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T07:09:50-07:00","id":1073098,"title":"","content":"The tone I usually get out of Scion is close to Superhero drama, with the world rather well aware of the heroes around them. Heroes tend to gather cults of celebrity, and deliver spectacular public beatdowns. I like the fact that there is no Masquerveil, because it creates a feeling that the whole world is pretty wacky, and the Gods are so close to us that Zeus can get Paparazzi'd by TMZ as he tries to stealthily exit a club to ditch the dude he just impregnated in a bathroom stall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><br /> I draw things! Wanna check it out? Click on the link below!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy</a><br /> <br /> <i><b>YES! I do commissions! </b></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/848-jtroy","name":"JTroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar848_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T08:43:40-07:00","id":1073147,"title":"","content":"The above would be a good example of what I don't like to see in scion to be perfectly honest (No offense to whatever your table likes).<br /> <br /> Scions are not Superhero's by nature, they are agents of the divine. Zeus is not a celebrity or a world leader, he's a God. Paparazzi is going to be rather difficult to engage in when most Deities are going to react to slander and insinuations with divine fury such as literally turning the person inside out and dangling them from a conspicuous location. Certainly there might be things that could be vaguely termed &quot;News&quot; but its probably not going to take the forms we'd associate with it today, considering a good portion of the populace is going to be actively worshiping said deity.<br /> <br /> &quot;Wacky&quot; is perhaps the opposite tone i'd like to see scion take, I imagine a much darker and more serious world...Realistic in some sense actually, as much as a fantasy world involving myth and legend can still be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T11:41:00-07:00","id":1073282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1070317-the-tone-of-scion?p=1073147#post1073147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The above would be a good example of what I don't like to see in scion to be perfectly honest (No offense to whatever your table likes).<br /> <br /> Scions are not Superhero's by nature, they are agents of the divine. Zeus is not a celebrity or a world leader, he's a God. Paparazzi is going to be rather difficult to engage in when most Deities are going to react to slander and insinuations with divine fury such as literally turning the person inside out and dangling them from a conspicuous location. Certainly there might be things that could be vaguely termed &quot;News&quot; but its probably not going to take the forms we'd associate with it today, considering a good portion of the populace is going to be actively worshiping said deity.<br /> <br /> &quot;Wacky&quot; is perhaps the opposite tone i'd like to see scion take, I imagine a much darker and more serious world...Realistic in some sense actually, as much as a fantasy world involving myth and legend can still be.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, trying a smear campaign against a deity who walks among you is probably in the top 5 list of most stupid things you can do in your life. If the god doesn't kill you personally, chances are their fanatical worshipers will.<br /> <br /> <br /> But honestly, if you pay attention to it, super heroes aren't too much better. I mean Dragon Ball Z at least had the common decency to take their fights to a deserted wasteland. Most other heroes let their fighting play out in the streets, causing thousands of dollars in property damage, not to mention the tax increase needed to repair everything, or the countless people they put in danger. I'm supposed to believe they can organize an evacuation order on a moment's notice and that nobody ever gets killed when somebody's punched through a skyscraper?<br /> <br /> <br /> But I also disagree with the concept of there not being a masquerade. I mean, you can play that way, if you want, but the game makes it pretty clear that exposing your powers to the public carries a risk of Fatebonds which everybody is afraid of. It's their incentive to not go crazy and just rip the world apart in a fit of anger. So if they do operate in the open, they're encouraged to maintain a low profile while doing so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-04-2017, 02:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T19:48:18-07:00","id":1073989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1070317-the-tone-of-scion?p=1073147#post1073147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The above would be a good example of what I don't like to see in scion to be perfectly honest (No offense to whatever your table likes).<br /> <br /> Scions are not Superhero's by nature, they are agents of the divine. Zeus is not a celebrity or a world leader, he's a God. Paparazzi is going to be rather difficult to engage in when most Deities are going to react to slander and insinuations with divine fury such as literally turning the person inside out and dangling them from a conspicuous location. Certainly there might be things that could be vaguely termed &quot;News&quot; but its probably not going to take the forms we'd associate with it today, considering a good portion of the populace is going to be actively worshiping said deity.<br /> <br /> &quot;Wacky&quot; is perhaps the opposite tone i'd like to see scion take, I imagine a much darker and more serious world...Realistic in some sense actually, as much as a fantasy world involving myth and legend can still be.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree that I probably could have avoided the W word. That was just, you know, bad on me. However...<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Marvel claims Thor, Loki, and the rest of the Aesir. DC claims Atlas and Samson(actually just a descendant of biblical Sammy, but he -does- have magic strongman hair). Rooted in Greco-Roman mythos, &quot;heralding the divine&quot; is pretty much the name of Wonder Woman's game.That, and getting bondaged. Superman has been referred to as &quot;the Messiah&quot;. The Sandman is an amazing comic series that's all about various mythologies coming together within the context of the larger DC Universe. Seriously, the story arc where all of the various pantheons come to place bids on Hell is some great stuff, the Sandman should practically be required reading. I could go on. Jeez, I didn't realize before this post just how completely full-to-the-brim DC was with Gods.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> So, Superheroes aren't necessarily Superheroes by nature either. But many of them -are- in fact Scions by nature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><br /> I draw things! Wanna check it out? Click on the link below!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy</a><br /> <br /> <i><b>YES! I do commissions! </b></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/848-jtroy","name":"JTroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar848_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T20:48:56-07:00","id":1074007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JTroy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1070317-the-tone-of-scion?p=1073989#post1073989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I agree that I probably could have avoided the W word. That was just, you know, bad on me. However...<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Marvel claims Thor, Loki, and the rest of the Aesir. DC claims Atlas and Samson(actually just a descendant of biblical Sammy, but he -does- have magic strongman hair). Rooted in Greco-Roman mythos, &quot;heralding the divine&quot; is pretty much the name of Wonder Woman's game.That, and getting bondaged. Superman has been referred to as &quot;the Messiah&quot;. The Sandman is an amazing comic series that's all about various mythologies coming together within the context of the larger DC Universe. Seriously, the story arc where all of the various pantheons come to place bids on Hell is some great stuff, the Sandman should practically be required reading. I could go on. Jeez, I didn't realize before this post just how completely full-to-the-brim DC was with Gods.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> So, Superheroes aren't necessarily Superheroes by nature either. But many of them -are- in fact Scions by nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>The natural response would be that very few if any of these comic-deities have much at all in common with their real world counterparts besides some inspiration of a power suite and their names, and Scion is explicitly a game of the latter.<br /> <br /> Comic Thor doesin't have the thought &quot;That guy just insulted me directly to my face, so I should probably maintain my honor by viciously murdering him....or his Father&quot; (granted i do have a liking for the gratuitous poetic smack talking, so there's that, but you get my point.<br /> <br /> Superhero's are inherently people and unless your going for a very edgy antihero vibe, they are generally people who stick firmly within the notions of conventional modern morality. Gods are however, not people. You can have a conversation about whether or not the Punishers actions are morally right or not, but that conversation looks alot different when the person's morality you are debating is Phobos Apollo, Born of the wolf, light of the sun, who's claim to moral correctness is &quot;Because i said so&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T21:25:16-07:00","id":1074011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JTroy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1070317-the-tone-of-scion?p=1073989#post1073989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, Superheroes aren't necessarily Superheroes by nature either. But many of them -are- in fact Scions by nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would have to say that if your considering Scions to be more or less identical to Superhero's, your probably not doing justice to the differences between them. Let me give an example.<br /> <br /> Superman is immensely powerful and skilled, he could destroy the earth and stop any threat against him. His stories therefore focus around his personal connections, what is right and wrong, what makes him...human, even though he is really a alien from another world, what matter is his internal humanity, he is a mortal man. But...in the grand scheme of things, Superman is also just some dude. He might be stronger and faster than you, but so is the Mountain and Usain Bolt. Nothing about him is innately special or different, he is quite literally just a mortal man.<br /> <br /> Most comics take this positions even when they involve being thats are properly deities. Marvel often gets around this issue by making them some form of alien or whatnot. This is not the case in Scion. Zeus is not an alien with the concerns and humanity of a mortal man, he is the living breathing King of Olympus, other Gods bow to him as sons do to their Father.<br /> <br /> In a nutshell, my position is that if your running around with little g gods, then your doing the core premise of the game a disservice (which is totally fine if you want to do it that way, YMMV) when the settings in involve big G Gods and their divine offspring on a quest to become the former.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T09:24:10-07:00","id":1074184,"title":"","content":"But you aren't playing Zeus, you're playing one of his innumerable bastards, with all the humanity being mostly human entails.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T09:33:13-07:00","id":1074191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JTroy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1070317-the-tone-of-scion?p=1073989#post1073989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I agree that I probably could have avoided the W word. That was just, you know, bad on me. However...<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Marvel claims Thor, Loki, and the rest of the Aesir. DC claims Atlas and Samson(actually just a descendant of biblical Sammy, but he -does- have magic strongman hair). Rooted in Greco-Roman mythos, &quot;heralding the divine&quot; is pretty much the name of Wonder Woman's game.That, and getting bondaged. Superman has been referred to as &quot;the Messiah&quot;. The Sandman is an amazing comic series that's all about various mythologies coming together within the context of the larger DC Universe. Seriously, the story arc where all of the various pantheons come to place bids on Hell is some great stuff, the Sandman should practically be required reading. I could go on. Jeez, I didn't realize before this post just how completely full-to-the-brim DC was with Gods.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> So, Superheroes aren't necessarily Superheroes by nature either. But many of them -are- in fact Scions by nature.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They have two <i>entire planets</i> populated by New Gods: Apocalypse (gods of evil) and New Genesis (gods of good). Plus they have <i>The Presence</i>, who is essentially the Abrahamic God, and they have the Old Gods who came before the creation of the New Gods. So, really, their pantheons span across the scope of the universe, rather than being limited to just the religions of earth.<br /> <br /> Marvel is even more confusing, because you've got the Gods, but then you've got Cosmic Beings, Celestials, Titans, Immortals, The Builders Infinity and so on. Many of those actually outrank the Gods, so it's hard to tell where they fit into the grand hierarchy of the universe.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> Personally, I find the idea of the New Gods in DC to be unsatisfying. Supposedly everybody from said planet is supposed to be a deity, and yet you see them cowed into submission to Darkseid who is prone to torture and straight up execution of anybody who displeases him. It's one thing to see a bunch of Gods be subservient, it's quite another to see the Gods treated like slaves. It detracts from the idea that they're supposed to be higher entities than mortals, if they receive the same treatment as everybody else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-06-2017, 12:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T10:08:56-07:00","id":1074205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1070317-the-tone-of-scion?p=1074184#post1074184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But you aren't playing Zeus, you're playing one of his innumerable bastards, with all the humanity being mostly human entails.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that Scion is not a game about being a quasi-magical bastard, its a game about divine offspring ascending to become demi-gods and then deities on their own right.<br /> <br /> Your trivializing something that is actually the core heart of the game and setting. If you just want to play some super powered blowoff with special abilities, the Aberrant game uses (almost, in 1E, the exact same in 2E) the exact same ruleset. Hell you could literally be be the child of the actual comic deities you want to emulate.<br /> <br /> Thats the difference between the game lines though, In scion, your not just a super powered by blow and Gods are not just dudes with special abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T11:12:36-07:00","id":1074239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1070317-the-tone-of-scion?p=1074205#post1074205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except that Scion is not a game about being a quasi-magical bastard, its a game about divine offspring ascending to become demi-gods and then deities on their own right.<br /> <br /> Your trivializing something that is actually the core heart of the game and setting. If you just want to play some super powered blowoff with special abilities, the Aberrant game uses (almost, in 1E, the exact same in 2E) the exact same ruleset. Hell you could literally be be the child of the actual comic deities you want to emulate.<br /> <br /> Thats the difference between the game lines though, In scion, your not just a super powered by blow and Gods are not just dudes with special abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not trivializing anything. If anything playing scions as being born with some higher authority instead of earning it cheapens the entire character arc. Hercules struggled against his temper and underwent nigh-impossible trials to make up for mistakes that any of the born-god Theoi would have barely dignified with shrugged shoulders and an &quot;opps&quot;. Yes it's about ascending to godhood, not being born with it. You have to shred mortal frailties, not just not be born with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T11:17:37-07:00","id":1074242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1070317-the-tone-of-scion?p=1074205#post1074205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except that Scion is not a game about being a quasi-magical bastard, its a game about divine offspring ascending to become demi-gods and then deities on their own right.</div> </div> </div> </div>How much of this is a matter of perspective, though? Like, does Hera have regard for Hercules as divine offspring, or is he just a loathsome bastard to her, some dude with special abilities? And does she see him the way that she does because of important Olympic Reasons, or because her shitty husband screwed around on her in the gutter again? And either way, does the distinction matter to Hercules? Is Wonder Woman just some girl with powers, or is she the blessed child of 6 Goddesses, formed from clay by Queen Hippolyta, the princess of the mythic Amazons? Why not both?<br /> <br /> I always thought that Scion 1E's system had been modelled after Exalted? I feel like it plays closer to a stripped-down Exalted. As for the Aberrant game... they're going to use the same system because they're going to have similar playstyles, I assumed. A lot of the things you can do in Aberrant you will(or at least should) also be able to do in Scion. The reasons and contexts for the things that you do will be different, but... the engine that powers the core heart of the game and setting -is-, as you said, identical to Aberrant. Surely this should not be disregarded.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><br /> I draw things! Wanna check it out? Click on the link below!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy</a><br /> <br /> <i><b>YES! I do commissions! </b></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/848-jtroy","name":"JTroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar848_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T12:36:53-07:00","id":1074274,"title":"","content":"I think Wonder Woman's abilities come from her magic armor and weapons, rather than her being born with them. For evidence, I present the fact that the Amazons held a competition for who would get to receive said armor and weapons and take on the mantle of Wonder Woman. Diana entered the competition under disguise (her mother forbade her) and won the tournament, thus being allowed to wear them and access the powers they granted her.<br /> <br /> In short, any of the Amazons could have become Wonder Woman. It's an electoral position that's earned through skill, not something you're born into.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T13:16:27-07:00","id":1074291,"title":"","content":"Used to be that she was made of clay, brought to life by the Olympian Gods through the prayers of Queen Hippolyta, and trained to be Themyscira's greatest warrior, who then went forth to kick Nazi ass. &quot;New 52&quot; changed her origins quite a bit, making her the secret daughter of Zeus. I'm not sure if &quot;Rebirth&quot; has changed things in her backstory even further, but, yeah. Daughter of Zeus, and currently ascended God of War.<br /> <br /> It seems like DC is -much- more comfortable with the basic concept of &quot;Gods&quot; than Marvel is, in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><br /> I draw things! Wanna check it out? Click on the link below!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy</a><br /> <br /> <i><b>YES! I do commissions! </b></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/848-jtroy","name":"JTroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar848_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T14:00:47-07:00","id":1074306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JTroy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1070317-the-tone-of-scion?p=1074291#post1074291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Used to be that she was made of clay, brought to life by the Olympian Gods through the prayers of Queen Hippolyta, and trained to be Themyscira's greatest warrior, who then went forth to kick Nazi ass. &quot;New 52&quot; changed her origins quite a bit, making her the secret daughter of Zeus. I'm not sure if &quot;Rebirth&quot; has changed things in her backstory even further, but, yeah. Daughter of Zeus, and currently ascended God of War.<br /> <br /> It seems like DC is -much- more comfortable with the basic concept of &quot;Gods&quot; than Marvel is, in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bRebirth appears to be bringing back the clay origin, though it hasn't been fully confirmed.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd no, Diana's powers have never been tied to her relics. In the Golden Age, her power came from &quot;Amazon Training&quot; which was a form of discipline that allowed her to channel psychic energy through her body, allowing her to perform superhuman feats. In the Silver Age, Bronze Age, and post-Crisis Age, her powers were blessings bestowed upon her by the gods. In the New 52, she became the daughter of Zeus, and her power came from that. Now, with Rebirth, we're not sure, but nothing has been said about her powers coming from objects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T14:28:12-07:00","id":1074316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JTroy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1070317-the-tone-of-scion?p=1074291#post1074291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems like DC is -much- more comfortable with the basic concept of &quot;Gods&quot; than Marvel is, in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>Read &quot;The Incredible Hercules&quot; series from a few years ago that came out of the World War Hulk event. It reminded me of why I'd always liked the character and delved a bit into the mythology and his relations with the other Greek gods. Also, Hercules leading a strike team of gods against the alien gods of the Skrull during the Secret Invasion event. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T16:02:15-07:00","id":1074372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElanConnor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1070317-the-tone-of-scion?p=1070569#post1070569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My idea is:<br /> <br /> Scion can really be everything<br /> <br /> I played it in very different style.<br /> <br /> - In MidleAge ( epic fantasy style, the real hero of the legends or vykings)<br /> - 1930 in america ( with a very deep noir tone, blackjack, alcohol and sigaretts, bossess issues etcetc)<br /> - Our days with all the light and dark of our community<br /> <br /> But what i prefer is... THE PULP ONE. Fuck i love pulp scion. Is like tarantino making a superhero movie, i just love it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Likewise, Scion can have any darn tone I want. Hey, I modeled my Scion campaign on Buffy the Vampire Slayer with equal parts Supernatural Action/Adventure and Teen Soap, with some Horror and Comedy (and Horror Comedy, it's a thing) mixed in. And of course, all filtered through mythology. I only regret I couldn't do an &quot;episode&quot; as a musical.<br /> <br /> I am less interested in what tone a game &quot;should&quot; have than in what I can do to give a game the tone I want.<br /> Dean Shomshak<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1175-dshomshak","name":"DShomshak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T19:55:22-07:00","id":1074475,"title":"","content":"I can do almost anything with Scion. It's one of those systems where I can take almost any genre, any trope, and I could tell an interesting story about it using mythology and the mechanics of Scion (with the Scion 2.0 houserules).<br /> <br /> I constantly find myself thinking &quot;That's a good example of Epic Manipulation&quot;, or &quot;That's a great use of a Knack&quot;, or &quot;That would make a fascinating titanspawn!&quot; whenever I am watching other media.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T20:40:22-07:00","id":1074496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DShomshak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1070317-the-tone-of-scion?p=1074372#post1074372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I only regret I couldn't do an &quot;episode&quot; as a musical.</div> </div> </div> </div>GM: Alright, now, your character's singing!<br /> Me: Oh trust me that is the <i>last</i> thing you want <i>me</i> to do. Like, I'm not allowed to sing anymore, court order.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T22:39:12-07:00","id":1074523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JTroy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1070317-the-tone-of-scion?p=1074291#post1074291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Used to be that she was made of clay, brought to life by the Olympian Gods through the prayers of Queen Hippolyta, and trained to be Themyscira's greatest warrior, who then went forth to kick Nazi ass. &quot;New 52&quot; changed her origins quite a bit, making her the secret daughter of Zeus. I'm not sure if &quot;Rebirth&quot; has changed things in her backstory even further, but, yeah. Daughter of Zeus, and currently ascended God of War.<br /> <br /> It seems like DC is -much- more comfortable with the basic concept of &quot;Gods&quot; than Marvel is, in general.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The whole &quot;amazonian training&quot; thing kind of bugs me. If her powers came from training, then it would stand to reason the entire island is full of super powered women. Yet I've never seen the Amazons being portrayed as anything other than immortal warriors of the classical Greek era. They don't seem to have any of Wonder Woman's powers in common except for possibly 1 Amazon who went rogue in the JLA cartoon. Also, during the Justice League cartoon, when Wonder Woman receives her armor, her mother says that they are relics blessed by the gods, which indicates the powers would have been stored within them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T06:28:14-07:00","id":1074625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1070317-the-tone-of-scion?p=1074523#post1074523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The whole &quot;amazonian training&quot; thing kind of bugs me. If her powers came from training, then it would stand to reason the entire island is full of super powered women. Yet I've never seen the Amazons being portrayed as anything other than immortal warriors of the classical Greek era. They don't seem to have any of Wonder Woman's powers in common except for possibly 1 Amazon who went rogue in the JLA cartoon. Also, during the Justice League cartoon, when Wonder Woman receives her armor, her mother says that they are relics blessed by the gods, which indicates the powers would have been stored within them.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bHer creator's original idea was to say that ANY woman can be a Wonder Woman. In the Golden Age, all Amazons could do what Diana could do. Diana was just the best of them, which is why she won the contest to return Steve Trevor to Man's World and become Wonder Woman.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd even after the Golden Age, the Amazons still do have super powers. They are just shown inconsistently because DC doesn't care about Wonder Woman or her world. Certainly not to the extent that they care about Batman and his world, at any rate. So the Amazons are often used for cannon fodder in stories and their powers are ignored or downplayed. You still see Amazons displaying super strength and other similar feats in stories that are showing any respect at all to Diana or her world.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd Diana has her powers with or without her relics, so they do not give her powers. We've seen her fight completely out of costume in the past. No difference.<br /> <br /> \u200bIf your only real exposure to Wonder Woman was the Justice League cartoon, then I'm sorry but you've never really experienced Wonder Woman. A lot of the more hardcore Wonder Woman fans hated her portrayal in that show. It has its fans, but it's FAR from the best portrayal of Wonder Woman by a country mile.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":679,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","user":"unnatural1","date":". 04-07-2017, 09:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T16:06:08-07:00","id":1074894,"title":"","content":"Like Iry, I find Scion one of the more flexible games from WW/OP. The two Scion campaigns I'd now like to run or play in... aren't Scion, they'd just use the game toward other ends. First, I'd like to use a revised Scion for a Dresden Files campaign. My gaming group tried DF:tRPG and found the system unplayable. (I understand this is *not* the fault of the underlying FATE system, which otherwise looks quite interesting.) But in looking for other game systems that could emulate the Dresdenverse and the aspects (ba-dum-bump) of DF:tRPG that we liked, Scion emerged at the top of my list.<br /> <br /> The other campaign I thought of, with the working title of Unreal City, is set in a world where the Gods withdrew long ago, but many of the lesser supernatural creatures were left behind. It's a bit WoD-ish, in that the setting includes vampires (more than one kind), shapeshifters, faeries and mortal mages, but I don't want to try kludging together up to half a dozen game systems. Scion seems like the game best suited to cover all the creatures of &quot;lower mythology&quot; at once.<br /> <br /> Dean Shomshak","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1175-dshomshak","name":"DShomshak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T16:57:20-07:00","id":1074908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1070317-the-tone-of-scion?p=1074475#post1074475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I constantly find myself thinking &quot;That's a good example of Epic Manipulation&quot;, or &quot;That's a great use of a Knack&quot;, or &quot;That would make a fascinating titanspawn!&quot; whenever I am watching other media.</div> </div> </div> </div>It has occurred to me that probably more than half the anime I've watched could in some way adapted to Scion. <br /> <br /> Also that it would be ridiculously easy to do some sort of Harry Potter/Percy Jackson/X-Men/Class of the Titans type &quot;Boarding School for Divinely-Touched Youth&quot;. <br /> <br /> Hmm. New Wave Scion, in which the Heroes who dwell in the modern 80s legends and epics of Wall Street, Scarface, Less Than Zero, Repo Man, Top Gun, Light of Day, The Legend of Billie Jean, and The Adventures of Buckaroo Banzai. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T11:24:09-07:00","id":1075188,"title":"","content":"Like most what others said, Scion is a very wide -literally and figurately speaking- rpg game.<br /> <br /> There are always the same questions asked by the players &quot;would thay knack or boon will be useful?&quot; for which there is no direct answer. Or rathee, there is right answer because it only depends on how players and Gm view Scion. <br /> <br /> The one thing important is not too be close minded because if your players would love something with more epic battles and less enigmas, you should listen . The system is very helpful in this way. There are multiple ways to play Scion, even in the same story with the same players. <br /> <br /> As epic as mythology is good but I think innovating and adding created material helps making this more interesting. A surprised player is always intrigued to look for more.<br /> <br /> As humouristic as marvel's movies is very helpful too. Delighted games make players comfortable. A tone too grave might ruin the mood of the game, players' or even yours if you play with rookies.<br /> <br /> As nasty as Game of thrones. Now, this, you have to be well prepared with lots of npcs. Maybe a less convincing tone because everything has to match. I won't go this way because I am not clever enough for that.<br /> <br /> Even a post apocalyptic game is ok. Because Titans came back and your players and a few Gods are still alive, give you opportunity to recreate the world as messing, as fantastic, as dark as you wish.<br /> <br /> <br /> There is no impossibilities in Scion. Every theme, every tone works. Delighted contemporay epic fantasy games remain my favorites with some dark moments to create greatness.<br /> <br /> <br /> Hope this helps <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}